  "notes": "Boot an NBA Fastbreak ROM from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released); the scenario names no game. Leave the fresh-NVRAM loop with Escape, wait out the power-up mechanism test and open the service menu. Run with PinMAME's built-in defender mechanism enabled (handle-mechanics 1): the ROM then shows no power-up report, so two Enters reach the main menu. Start T.16 MOTOR TEST, let its automatic self-test run with a frame every 1.5 s, then select each following item with Up and run it with Enter, taking a frame every second. The test names the defender position optos it reads; the defender motor outputs 37/38 and the position switches 51-55 are captured as transitions.",
